 {
  "key": "logic.truth-tables.q04",
  "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
  "concepts": [
   "comp.logic.truth-tables"
  ],
  "difficulty": 3,
  "marks": 1,
  "estimatedSeconds": 60,
  "stem": "For which inputs is the output of `X = (A AND NOT B) OR C` equal to **0**?",
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "content": "A = 1, B = 0, C = 0",
    "rationale": "A AND NOT B = 1 AND 1 = 1, so X = 1."
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "content": "A = 0, B = 1, C = 1",
    "rationale": "C = 1, so the OR gives X = 1."
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "content": "A = 1, B = 1, C = 0",
    "correct": true,
    "rationale": "Correct: NOT B = 0, so A AND NOT B = 0; with C = 0 the OR gives 0."
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "content": "A = 1, B = 1, C = 1",
    "rationale": "C = 1, so X = 1."
   }
  ],
  "explanation": "X = 0 needs both parts of the OR to be 0: C = 0 and (A AND NOT B) = 0. Among the options only A = 1, B = 1, C = 0 does this. Output column: 01011101.",
  "hints": [
   "X is 1 whenever C = 1, so look at rows with C = 0.",
   "Then A AND NOT B must also be 0."
